<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Paros</h1><p class="st-meta">900 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.) · capital Paros</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Cycladic island famed for its fine white marble and its poet Archilochus, and coloniser of Thasos.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Paros, in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyclades">Cyclades</a>, was settled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionia">Ionian Greeks</a> in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>. Its translucent marble, quarried in underground galleries, became the prized stone of Greek sculptors. By the 7th century BCE Paros was strong enough to colonise <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thasos">Thasos</a> c. 680 BCE and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parion">Parion</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellespont">Hellespont</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archilochus">Archilochus</a>, a pioneering lyric and iambic poet, was a Parian who joined the settlement of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thasos">Thasos</a>. Paros was a commercial and religious centre with a temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demeter">Demeter</a>. It supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> in 490 BCE, and the Athenian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miltiades">Miltiades</a> failed to take it in 489 BCE. In the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/delian-league">Delian League</a> Paros paid one of the largest island tributes.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Paros came under Hellenistic kings and later Roman control by 146 BCE. Its inscribed Parian Chronicle of 264 BCE, now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a>, is a key source for Greek chronology, and Parian marble remained in demand.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 900 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem